Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"compactness1","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"concavity1","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"concave_points1","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"symmetry1","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"fractal_dimension1","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"radius2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"texture2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"perimeter2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"area2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"smoothness2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"compactness2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"concavity2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"concave_points2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"symmetry2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"fractal_dimension2","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"radius3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"texture3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"perimeter3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"area3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"smoothness3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"compactness3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"concavity3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"concave_points3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"symmetry3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"},{"name":"fractal_dimension3","role":"Feature","type":"Continuous","demographic":null,"description":null,"units":null,"missing_values":"no"}],"additional_info":{"summary":"Features are computed from a digitized image of a fine needle aspirate (FNA) of a breast mass.  They describe characteristics of the cell nuclei present in the image. A few of the images can be found at http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~street/images/\r\n\r\nSeparating plane described above was obtained using Multisurface Method-Tree (MSM-T) [K. P. Bennett, \"Decision Tree Construction Via Linear Programming.\" Proceedings of the 4th Midwest Artificial Intelligence and Cognitive Science Society, pp. 97-101, 1992], a classification method which uses linear programming to construct a decision tree.  Relevant features were selected using an exhaustive search in the space of 1-4 features and 1-3 separating planes.\r\n\r\nThe actual linear program used to obtain the separating plane in the 3-dimensional space is that described in: [K. P. Bennett and O. L. Mangasarian: \"Robust Linear Programming Discrimination of Two Linearly Inseparable Sets\", Optimization Methods and Software 1, 1992, 23-34].\r\n\r\nThis database is also available through the UW CS ftp server:\r\nftp ftp.cs.wisc.edu\r\ncd math-prog/cpo-dataset/machine-learn/WDBC/","purpose":null,"funded_by":null,"instances_represent":null,"recommended_data_splits":null,"sensitive_data":null,"preprocessing_description":null,"variable_info":"1) ID number\r\n2) Diagnosis (M = malignant, B = benign)\r\n3-32)\r\n\r\nTen real-valued features are computed for each cell nucleus:\r\n\r\n\ta) radius (mean of distances from center to points on the perimeter)\r\n\tb) texture (standard deviation of gray-scale values)\r\n\tc) perimeter\r\n\td) area\r\n\te) smoothness (local variation in radius lengths)\r\n\tf) compactness (perimeter^2 / area - 1.0)\r\n\tg) concavity (severity of concave portions of the contour)\r\n\th) concave points (number of concave portions of the contour)\r\n\ti) symmetry \r\n\tj) fractal dimension (\"coastline approximation\" - 1)","citation":null}}}